Infrastructure & Platform

AI infrastructure and platform companies building the tools other AI engineers rely on — model serving, evaluation, and orchestration at the frontier.

Salary premium

+18–30%

Hiring

Medium

Must have
Model evaluation framework design

Platform companies build the eval harnesses that other teams depend on, so evaluation methodology itself becomes the product, not an internal QA step.

Must have
Inference optimization (batching, quantization, caching)

Serving models at platform scale means every millisecond and token of latency multiplies across millions of requests, making inference efficiency a core engineering discipline.

Must have
Agent orchestration and tool-use architecture

Infra companies design the frameworks that let AI systems call tools and chain steps reliably, requiring deep understanding of failure modes across multi-step agent runs.

Important
Fine-tuning and RLHF pipeline engineering

Building the infrastructure that other companies use to customize models requires hands-on experience with training pipelines most application engineers never touch.

Important
Context window and token economy management

Platform tools are used by engineers optimizing their own costs, so understanding token-level tradeoffs deeply enough to expose them as product features is expected.

