Start here this week

This week: build a RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) application on a document set you actually care about. Not a tutorial RAG on sample data — your own documents, your own use case. Evaluate the retrieval quality honestly. Note where it fails. Ship it somewhere people can use it. That project is worth ten certifications.

For structured entry, DeepLearning.AI's short courses on LLM application development cover the core toolkit (prompt engineering, RAG, agents, function calling) systematically. Pair them with reading the Anthropic and OpenAI documentation directly — the API docs tell you what the models can actually do, not what the course assumes they do. The gap is instructive.

